# Solo Channel chat pane and the offline slash commands.
# Title -> main menu -> Play now -> world splash -> Choose Your World -> Evergreen -> the Well ->
# N = New Soul, name, RETURN -> the map. Then click the chat splitter grip (the default pane is
# (0,420,640,60) with a 4px grip at y 420..424) and type the commands.
# requires: map_enter chat_pane chat_command chat_say springy_object
# requires-match: chat_command cmd=springy arg=\S+ state=loaded
# requires-match: chat_command cmd=version arg= state=shown
# requires-match: chat_say text=Well of Souls Version 1\.0
# The title screen turns any key into the main menu, so no boot_menu expect is needed.
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 30
# Three states before the Well, not two: 1 main menu -> 2 the
# "Where Do You Want To Play Today?" splash (FUN_0041D31F) -> 3 the world
# list (FUN_0041D717). The original's own table is FUN_0041B891 (all.c:21078);
# the port used to collapse the splash, so the script had drifted. RETURN is
# the plan's keyboard shortcut for the row click (msg 0x474).
wait 20
key x
wait 40
# Choose Your World: the world rows are FUN_0041D3CC's list, x = 2*((W+7)>>3) = 160,
# y = H/20 + ((H+3)>>2) = 144, step 0 at 640x480; FUN_00405153 then scales by client/1000,
# so the Evergreen row rect is (102,69)-(174,77).
click 120 73
expect world_chosen 300
key n
wait 5
# The New Soul name field needs a click to take focus (front.c name_rect = 104,88,432,26).
click 200 100
wait 2
text Tester
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
# Incarnating on link 0 puts the hero on the link, so the map walks into it (FUN_00462958).
# Click a far corner of the walk rect on the next frame to step off the link first.
click 60 240
wait 60
# Open the chat pane from its splitter grip. The hero is standing on link 0, so the command
# block runs back to back: the map walks into the link a few frames after map_enter.
click 320 422
expect chat_pane 120
text /springy
key RETURN
expect springy_object 120
text /version
key RETURN
expect chat_say 120
quit
